      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Same problem here, when trying to test with multiple clients only one will join the correct instance, the rest will stay on a blackscreen for a while until they eventually make their own instance automatically, which isn't wanted here. I also get the same message in the logs. This used to work before just fine for me. Leaving this unfixed will just cause people to upload broken worlds since they can't test and see if things get synced correctly, which can also in some cases cause crashes. Hope this gets fixed hopefully soon. Until then the only way to test worlds is to actually upload, which takes time and depending on the upload speed of someone could take a long time, then launch the clients manually and again manually join the same world with all of them. \n\nThing is this isn't even the SDKs fault, because when downgrading to the older version where this worked just fine it also doesn't work anymore so there's probably something wrong with vrchat internally.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
