  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "There has always been this problem, but in this latest update it seems that the situation has worsened. Before this update, when I went to try my world on 2 or more clients, it happened that sometimes it didn't work, so sometimes it brought me back to the home or took me to a new instance, but it happened a few times, so you could still work on it. With this latest update it seems that it doesn't work anymore, it's been more than an hour that I'm trying but I haven't been able to make it work, I've also tried to create a completely empty scene but every time a client enters correctly, the other one stays for a while with a black screen and loads on a new instance of the same world.\nAnother detail, when I go to close the two clients one closes correctly, the other crashes and creates a log (here I don't see the possibility of attaching files, so if it's useful I will send it to support).\n\nAnd lastly, every time I use multiple clients, the worlds I have visited and downloaded previously are deleted or not used anyway, so I have to download them again, which is a bit frustrating, especially for those with a slow connection, so I don't have the freedom to use this function whenever I want\n\nEDIT: Looking on the log of the client I noticed that the second client give me an \"OnJoinRoomFailed\" instantly when I press \"Go\", and I tried even to clear the cache and playerPref, but still nothing changed",
